      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Storage Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with AWS S3 as the managed object storage provider for this task. I'll be leveraging the `boto3` library to interact with S3 within the `object_metadata.py` Python file. This should give me the functionality I need to read the metadata.\n\n\n**Implementing Object Metadata**\n\nI am now actively implementing the `object_metadata.py` file, focusing on the core function. It'll take bucket and key as inputs, leveraging `boto3` to fetch object metadata from AWS S3. The design is straightforward; the function will return the relevant metadata upon successful retrieval.\n\n\n",
