      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Object Storage Options**\n\nOkay, I'm leaning toward AWS S3. It seems the most straightforward route, given its popularity and built-in support for generating presigned URLs. The objective is to create a Python file, `presigned_download.py`, so I have a good framework. My focus now is on the Python implementation itself.\n\n\n**Implementing the Script**\n\nI'm now deep in the implementation of the `presigned_download.py` script. The goal is a function that crafts time-limited, signed URLs for S3 objects, leveraging `boto3`. I'm focused on the input parameters \u2013 bucket, object name, expiry \u2013 and the correct use of the `boto3` library's `generate_presigned_url` method to generate the URL.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789821204907,
          "start": 1789821203233
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9a83321001CAFqV7pj75DjXC",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9a82d630014HaYQLtOw0QPfs",
      "session_id": "ses_f4657d2aeffeIgaiAWYch7lyJq",
